  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-110102",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- To find the slope of the line $2x-4y=8,$ we convert to slope-intercept form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-4y & =8 \\\\ -4y & =-2x+8 \\\\ 4y & =2x-8 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- To find the slope of the line $kx+2y=12,$ we convert to slope-intercept form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kx+2y & =12 \\\\ 2y & =-kx+12 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{k}{2}x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $-\\frac{k}{2}.$\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have $-\\frac{k}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ We solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{k}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{k}{2} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-110102\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p> For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>To find the slope of the line <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"76\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> we convert to slope-intercept form, as follows:\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"77\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 8.19em;\"><mjx-table><mjx-itable><mjx-mtr><mjx-mtd style=\"text-align: right; padding-right: 0px; padding-bottom: 0.3em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" spac